UID:cgr6co9lcopj0bb4ccq64b9kcpgm6b9p64s6ab9k6pi30d1ic5i64d9gco@google.com
CREATED:20201026T223421Z
DESCRIPTION:Event: https://fb.me/e/cKJqoMFq7\n\nAfter a long year\, Music i
 s Art will be hosting the first Alliance concert of 2020! Join us at the le
 gendary Sportsmen's Tavern for a night of incredible energy and songwriting
  from members of the WNY Music Industry Alliance - PA Line\, Philip Stephen
 \, and Julian Burgio. \n\nTickets are $15 and will be sold in tables of 2\,
  4\, or 6. Click the link to make your reservation: https://www.showclix.co
 m/event/mia-presents-pa-line-w-stephen-burgio\n\nMasks are required when no
 t seated\, and tables and chairs may not be moved. It's a strange world we'
 re living in\, but thank goodness we can finally enjoy a little live music!
 \n\nwww.musicisart.org\n\nPA Line - Original music inspired by Grass Roots\
 , infused with Soul\, and born from the Indie scene. PA Line is Peace Alway
 s. www.PALineband.com\n\nPhilip Stephen - One part punk\, one part eloquent
  storyteller. facebook.com/philipstephenmusic\n\nJulian Burgio - Singer/Son
 gwriter based in Buffalo\, New York with influences across the spectrum fro
 m The Beatles to Death Cab For Cutie. www.facebook.com/julianburgiomusic
LAST-MODIFIED:20201026T223421Z
LOCATION:Sportsmens Tavern
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MiA Presents: PA Line\, Philip Stephen\, & Julian Burgio
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
