CREATED:20220309T150245Z
DESCRIPTION:Event: fb://event/333459015354617\n\nArmchair Boogie makes thei
 r Buffalo Iron Works debut on Tuesday\, March 15th\, 2022!\n\nTickets: $10 
 ADV/$15 DOS\nAges: 18+\nDoors: 7:00pm\nShow: 8:00pm\n\nABOUT ARMCHAIR BOOGI
 E:\nStarting in 2015 from a front porch in the college town of Stevens Poin
 t\, Wisconsin\, Armchair Boogie can be defined by their pickin’ skills and 
 infectious grooves. Augie Dougherty (banjo\, vocals) and Ben Majeska (guita
 r\, vocals) began playing under the name prior to the addition of Eli Fried
 ers (bass) and solidification of Denzel Connor (drums) as the driving rhyth
 m section behind a bluegrass\, up-tempo\, jammin-funkgrass outfit.\n\nIn th
 e spring of 2018 Armchair Boogie moved to Madison\, WI and released their f
 irst album. During this time they began touring around Wisconsin\, the Midw
 est\, and across America. Their journeys on the road have led them to stage
 s such as Blue Ox\, Northwest String Summit\, John Hartford Memorial Festiv
 al\, Summer Camp\, and Live on King Street. They’ve had the honor to share 
 the stage with The Infamous Stringdusters\, Horseshoes and Hand Grenades\, 
 The Dead South\, Kitchen Dwellers\, Pert Near Sandstone\, Trout Steak Reviv
 al\, and have jammed with many more.\n\nWith the help of a loving and dedic
 ated following\, the group was able to successfully crowdfund their album\,
  “What Does Time Care?”\, which was released with a sold out show at the Hi
 gh Noon Saloon in Madison on October 11\, 2019. The band is surging into 20
 20 supporting acts such as The Infamous Stringdusters and Kitchen Dwellers 
 and appearing at Leftover Salmon’s Boogie At The Broadmoor. Armchair Boogie
  will return to Blue Ox\, Northwest String Summit\, and Boats and Bluegrass
  in 2020.\n\nFunk Grass Americana pushing the boundaries of a broadly defin
 ed genre!\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20220309T150245Z
LOCATION:Buffalo Iron Works
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Armchair Boogie at Buffalo Iron Works | MAR 15
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
