DESCRIPTION:Band: PA LINE\nStage: Lakeside Lawn Stage 1\nTime: 6:30pm\nSet 
 Length: 45 minutes\n\nFor full details on load in\, parking\, and more\, CL
 ICK HERE:\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1aXF43yopqx5f1jP97RdCZPUeBx
 hOvnb0JjvxoSUyaPU/edit?usp=sharing\n\n2025 Music is Art Festival - \nPerfor
 mer Guidelines \nCongratulations - you've been selected to perform at this 
 year’s Music is Art Festival\, taking place at Terminal B and Buffalo's Out
 er Harbor. Please read the following information carefully to ensure a smoo
 th\, successful experience. \nARRIVAL & CHECK-IN\n Please arrive 2 hours be
 fore your scheduled set time. Check in directly with your Stage Manager upo
 n arrival. Set times are confirmed at check-in and may be subject to change
 . If you have specific production needs\, bring a stage plot/input list to 
 assist the production crew. \nSTAGE & PRODUCTION\n All stages provide PA\, 
 monitors\, and full backline (except for backline at Songwriter Row) - thes
 e must be used. Performers must bring their own instruments and instrument 
 cables. \nBackline includes:\n - Full drum kit (with cymbals\, hi-hats\, an
 d double pedal adapter)\n - Bass amp\n - 3 guitar amps\n - Note: Keyboards\
 , stands\, and benches must be supplied by the artist. \nPA includes:\n - F
 OH and monitor mixes\n - Mics\, mic stands\, and DIs\n - A dedicated sound 
 engineer at each stage\n\n Artists using backing tracks will be informed in
  advance of format requirements.\nPARKING & LOAD-IN\n Each act will receive
  one free parking pass\, valid at the Terminal B Lot. Pick up your pass sta
 rting August 14 at Jack Rabbit (1010 Elmwood Ave) during business hours. \n
 - If you're playing the Skate Park Stage\, its best to unload at 702 Fuhrma
 nn Blvd and then move your vehicle.\n\n - If you're playing the Bell Slip S
 tage\, its best to unload at 575 Fuhrmann Blvd and then move your vehicle.\
 n\n - All other stage locations should unload directly from the Terminal B 
 lot (850 Fuhrmann Blvd)\nStaff and volunteers will be available to direct y
 ou to your location. For DOS questions or concerns\, call or text Sara Eliz
 abeth at (716) 515-5637.\nPlease bring only essential gear - instruments\, 
 cables\, pedalboards\, drumsticks\, etc. You may use carts or wagons for tr
 ansport. No motorized vehicles. No storage is available at stages. Unattend
 ed items are left at your own risk. \nPERFORMER HOSPITALITY\n The Musicians
 ' Lounge is backstage at Terminal B and includes food\, drinks\, and games.
  Performer-only wristbands are available at the lounge entrance. Guests are
  not permitted. \nSET-UP & STAGE ETIQUETTE\n Each stage has a Stage Manager
  who controls the schedule and logistics. Please follow their instructions.
  \nAt Terminal B (double stage):\n - One band plays while the next sets up 
 on the other half.\n - Do not make noise or adjust stage equipment until cl
 eared by the Stage Manager.\n - Techs will assist with setup and sound chec
 k.\n - Have instruments tuned and ready. At your set time\, your engineer w
 ill perform a quick line check and then it’s go time.\nAt all other stages:
 \n - Standard changeover is 15 minutes. Same rules apply. \nPERFORMANCE CON
 DUCT\n - Play your heart out - this festival is for you!\n - Maintain reaso
 nable stage volume to support the best sound mix.\n - This is a family-frie
 ndly event. Please use discretion with language and behavior. Music is Art 
 reserves the right to end any set that violates community standards. \nAFTE
 R YOUR SET\n - Remove all equipment and personal items immediately after yo
 ur set.\n - Stage Techs will assist if needed.\n - No gear may be left at t
 he stage - anything left unattended is at your own risk. \nThank you - we a
 re thrilled to have you as part of the 23rd Annual Music is Art Festival! Y
 our talent and energy make this event what it is\, and we can't wait to see
  you perform! \n\nSara Elizabeth\nMusic is Art Program Director\nAssistant 
 Festival Coordinator\nsaraelizabeth@musicisart.org\n716-515-5637
LAST-MODIFIED:20250915T213516Z
LOCATION:Outer Harbor Buffalo\, 225 Fuhrmann Boulevard\, Buffalo\, NY 14203
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Music is Art Festival
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
