DESCRIPTION:4:00p-5p\n\n$1100\n\nRandal Miller\nDirector of Programming\nPi
 ttsburgh Cultural Trust\n803 Liberty Ave\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15222\n412-471-5
 120\nMiller@trustarts.org | TrustArts.org\n\nTest one two.\nHello Trever!\n
 \nWe're very excited to have you perform for our Three Rivers Arts Festival
  this year! Thank you for being with us and helping to make it happen. Here
  are some advance details for your performance. Please let us know if you h
 ave any questions. Our questions are highlighted below. Please reply all wh
 en answering.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nArtist: PA Line\n\nDate: Sunday\, June 7\n\nLo
 ad in & Sound Check: 3:00 PM\n\nPerformance Time: 4:00 PM - 5:00 PM\n\n\n\n
 ON-SITE CONTACT\n\nI will be your on-site contact for the day and my number
  is (412) 979-4719.\nCall or text if you have any questions on the performa
 nce day.\nPlease reach out if you are running late.\nIf you have questions 
 regarding the performance before your arrival time\, please direct them via
  email to me.\n\n>> Please provide an on-site contact name and number.\n\n\
 nSTAGE SPECS\nThe stage will be a 40' w x 20' d x 3' h stage deck with 2 st
 airs and loading platform.\nDirectly to the left off-stage will be the moni
 tor/tech world. \nPlease note there is minimal storage space on stage. Any 
 guitars\, keyboard setups\, etc should plan on being held offstage. \nThere
  is a festival banner that hangs upstage\, and the stage does not have the 
 capabilities to rig additional backdrops.\n>> Please see the attached rende
 rings/images of the stage area.\n\n>> Please send a copy of your stage plot
  and/or input list ASAP\n\nPA & LX SPECS\nPlease see the attached PA Spec d
 ocument.\nNote\, due to this event being held outdoors and the way the sun 
 sets\, lights are usually not very noticeable/effective until the last few 
 songs of the headliner performance. House lights are the sun and cannot be 
 dimmed on command.\nBACKLINE\nNo backline will be provided for this show. Y
 ou are responsible for bringing all of your own instruments including drums
 .\nWe will have dedicated stage hands to help set up as needed.\nPARKING & 
 ARRIVAL\n\nA map of the stage and parking area is attached.\nParking/Artist
  Entrance will be available off of Fort Duquesne Blvd & 9th St (directly be
 hind the stage) and will only be valid during your load-in\, performance\, 
 and load-out times.\nParking is only available for band members. Family\, f
 riends\, and photographers must find their own parking elsewhere.\nParking 
 is very limited. Please do your best to carpool\, as there is only room for
  2-3 vehicles. Other vehicles must find parking elsewhere.\nPlease see the 
 attached parking passes.\n\n>> If you are driving to the venue\, can you le
 t me know exactly what kind and # of vehicles you are traveling in?\n\n>> P
 lease let me know if you are traveling in a truck or van if applicable\n\nB
 ACKSTAGE & HOSPITALITY\nA trailer directly behind the stage will serve as a
  green room. The trailer is shared between groups throughout the festival d
 ay\, but will be accessible to your group during soundcheck and performance
  times. \nThe green room trailer is climate controlled and equipped with ru
 nning water\, a bathroom\, sink\, kitchenette\, chairs\, etc.\nMISCELLANEOU
 S\nWe have dedicated stage hands\nThis is a free event – no guest list requ
 ired!\nThis is a family event – no profanity of any kind\, both lyrical and
  dialogue between songs.\nEngagement is a free\, non-ticketed\, outdoor fes
 tival in a public park. Purchaser is unable to restrict audience members fr
 om using recording devices.\nIn Summary\, I'm looking for the following fro
 m your end:\nConfirmation of sound check / load in times.\nA best on-site p
 hone number\nA current stage plot & input list ASAP\nCan you let me know ex
 actly what kind and # of the vehicles you are traveling in?\nPlease let me 
 know if you are traveling in a truck or van if applicable\nThanks\,\n\nZach
  Mitchell\n(he/him)\nFlyspace Productions\nEvent Manager\nwww.flyspaceprodu
 ctions.com\no: 412.208.3020 | c: 412.979.4719\nf: 412.533.5745 | @flyspacep
 rod\nzachary@flyspaceproductions.com\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet
 : https://meet.google.com/fiw-moqa-hxy\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https:/
 /support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease do not edit this secti
 on.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
